ach."] [124 1 "// superLookup is lookupAttr over the part of start's MRO after typ (super's lookup)."] [153 1 "// descrGet is a found attribute's __get__ (obj nil: from the class); a built-in method found on a"] [154 1 "// built-in type is bound to obj (its value for a built-in subclass's instance)."] [160 3 "// object's methods take the instance itself (PY6d's REQUEST: __reduce_ex__'s class); objectDescr is"] [161 3 "// methodDescrs[b] == ObjectType without the map's lookup on every method's binding (queue 210)"] [173 1 "// methodDescrs are the built-in types' methods that left their type's dict through the class (T.name: CPython's"] [174 1 "// method_descriptor), each with its type: put in a class's dict (socket.socket.getsockname = saved, test_socket's"] [175 1 "// test_injected_authentication_failure) such a method still binds to the instance, as a method descriptor does,"] [176 1 "// where a built-in function there (class A: f = len) does not."] [181 1 "// instanceDict is o's __dict__, nil when it has none."] [202 1 "// The attribute instructions' inline caches (202b; PEP 659's LOAD_ATTR and STORE_ATTR caches, after the type"] [203 1 "// version tag): load-attr and store-attr of an object whose type takes the generic path keep, per instruction, the"] [204 1 "// type they last saw and lookupAttr's answer for it, valid while typeEpoch has not moved (the epoch the type"] [205 1 "// attribute cache's own answers hold by, attr.go's lookupAttr), so a hit compares two words where lookupAttr hashes"] [206 1 "// the name into the type's cache."] [212 2 "// di: where the instance's dict held the name when it was last found there (queue 210; CPython's"] [213 2 "// LOAD_ATTR_INSTANCE_VALUE's index): an entry holding the name's very str (co_names are interned) is the name's"] [217 1 "// lookupAttrAt is lookupAttr(tp, name) through the cache of c's instruction pc."] [223 1 "// attrSite is an instruction's caches: the last types it saw, the latest first (queue 210: richards' four task"] [224 1 "// classes share their methods' instructions, and one entry missed at every change of type)."] [229 1 "// attrICAt is c's instruction pc's cache entry holding lookupAttr(tp, name)."] [251 34 "// tp's old entry, else the oldest, dropped"] [256 1 "// dictEntryAt is the position of the entry of d holding name itself, through the hint *di (kept up to date); -1"] [257 1 "// when d does not hold name (an equal str in its place is found, but not kept as the hint)."] [269 1 "// loadAttrAt is load-attr at c's instruction pc: GetAttr, its generic path's lookup through the instruction's cache."] [278 3 "// genericGetAttrFound's instance dict through the hint (queue 210)"] [300 1 "// storeAttrAt is store-attr (v nil: delete-attr) at c's instruction pc: SetAttr, its generic path's lookup through"] [301 1 "// the instruction's cache."] [310 3 "// genericSetAttrFound's dict.Set through the hint: a value replaced in place (queue 210)"] [319 21 "// the usual case: the name inserted last"] [326 1 "// GenericGetAttr is object.__getattribute__."] [333 1 "// genericGetAttrFound is GenericGetAttr with lookupAttr's answer for o's type tp."] [351 1 "// GenericSetAttr is object.__setattr__ (v nil: object.__delattr__)."] [358 1 "// genericSetAttrFound is GenericSetAttr with lookupAttr's answer for o's type tp."] [386 1 "// typeGetAttr is type.__getattribute__: the metatype's data descriptors, then the type's MRO, then"] [387 1 "// the metatype's other attributes."] [399 29 "// a method descriptor leaving its type"] [417 1 "// typeSetAttr is type.__setattr__: a class's attribute, its slots updated for a special one."] [428 3 "// tp_name: a static type's module and name ('compression.zstd.ZstdCompressor'; builtins' bare)"] [448 1 "// SetAttr is setattr(o, name, v); v nil is delattr."] [456 1 "// DelAttr is delattr(o, name)."] [459 1 "// GetAttrOptional is getattr(o, name) with nil, not an AttributeError, when there is no such attribute."] [462 1 "// LookupSpecial is a special method's lookup on o's type (_PyObject_LookupSpecial): bound to o, or nil."] [471 1 "// getAttrOptional is getattr(o, name, None) without the None: nil when there is no such attribute."] [483 1 "// callBound calls a method found on self's type bound to self (CPython's vectorcall of an unbound"] [484 1 "// method with self first, or __get__ then the call); owner is the type of self's MRO it was found on"] [485 1 "// (lookupAttr's), nil when not known."] [494 4 "// a built-in function in a class's dict is no method descriptor: called without the instance, as"] [495 4 "// descrGet's rule and lookup_maybe_method (class C: __call__ = len; typing.NewType's __call__ = _idfunc,"] [496 4 "// queue 207)"] [500 4 "// object's own methods take the instance itself (descrGet's rule, PY6d's R2), as for"] [501 4 "// object.__reduce_ex__ of a class deriving from a built-in type (PY6g's F2: random.Random's pickling)"] [554 2 "// a descriptor's own attributes (PY6a: inspect's getattr_static reads __name__ and __objclass__)"] [567 2 "// object's attributes"] [602 2 "// BaseException's attributes (exceptions.c's BaseException_getset and members)"] [661 1 "// unpackAll is the items of an iterable."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[81 31] [108 31] [112 28] [116 35] [128 6] [128 20] [134 9] [134 23] [137 31] [141 28] [145 35] [156 26] [167 33] [237 23] [259 18] [277 27] [285 41] [309 27] [311 21] [315 32] [318 34] [339 28] [362 34] [396 33] [397 27] [406 34] [423 35] [439 38] [450 32] [508 33] [529 18] [547 27] [585 26] [644 58]]} (go/file "attr.go" :imports [

